1. Connection

Endpoint: [xxxx-ats.iot.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com]
Port: 8883 (MQTT over TLS, mutual authentication)
Region: ap-south-1 (Mumbai)
MQTT client ID: the device’s thing name (listed below)
QoS: 1
2. Certificates (attached)

Each device has its own set:

[thingName]-certificate.pem.crt – device certificate
[thingName]-private.pem.key – device private key
AmazonRootCA1.pem – Amazon Root CA, used to verify our server
3. Topic
        trucks/{thingName}/temperature
        Each device may publish only to its own topic. For example, device TRUCK-1 publishes to          trucks/TRUCK-1/temperature. Publishing to any other topic will be refused.

4. Message format (JSON)
   {
     "ts": "2026-10-28T10:00:00Z",
     "temp": 4.2,
     "unit": "C",
     "lat": 12.97,
     "lng": 77.59
   }